.TH ASPEN-GENERATE-ENV 8 "" "aspen-discovery" "Aspen Discovery"
.SH NAME
aspen-generate-env \- write the environment file a systemd unit consumes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aspen-generate-env
.I service
.I site
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads the site's config.ini and writes
.IR /run/aspen/<site>/<service>.env ,
so per-site settings reach the unit without hand-maintained environment
files. Run as an ExecStartPre by the unit itself. The only
.I service
currently is
.BR solr ,
whose file carries SOLR_PORT (from solrPort) and SOLR_MEM (from the
optional solrMemory, default 3g), both from the [Index] section.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aspen-create-dirs (8)
